  "body": "## Vulnerability Details\n\nThe Router contract implements slippage protection via `calculatedAmountThreshold` parameters but lacks deadline/expiry protection. Without a deadline parameter, a submitted transaction can remain in the mempool indefinitely and be executed at any future time, potentially when market conditions have changed significantly.\n\nAll swap functions in the Router are affected:\n\n```solidity\nfunction swap(PoolKey memory poolKey, SwapParameters params, int256 calculatedAmountThreshold)\n    public payable returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate) { ... }\n\nfunction swap(PoolKey memory poolKey, SwapParameters params, int256 calculatedAmountThreshold, address recipient)\n    public payable returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate) { ... }\n\nfunction swap(PoolKey memory poolKey, bool isToken1, int128 amount, SqrtRatio sqrtRatioLimit, uint256 skipAhead,\n    int256 calculatedAmountThreshold, address recipient) public payable returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate) { ... }\n\nfunction swap(PoolKey memory poolKey, bool isToken1, int128 amount, SqrtRatio sqrtRatioLimit, uint256 skipAhead,\n    int256 calculatedAmountThreshold) public payable returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate) { ... }\n\nfunction swap(PoolKey memory poolKey, bool isToken1, int128 amount, SqrtRatio sqrtRatioLimit, uint256 skipAhead)\n    public payable returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate) { ... }\n\nfunction swap(RouteNode memory node, TokenAmount memory tokenAmount, int256 calculatedAmountThreshold)\n    public payable returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate) { ... }\n\nfunction multihopSwap(Swap memory s, int256 calculatedAmountThreshold)\n    public payable returns (PoolBalanceUpdate[] memory balanceUpdates) { ... }\n```\n\nNone of these functions include a `deadline` parameter to enforce transaction expiry.\n\n\n## Impact\n\nThis is a critical UX/security flaw affecting every swap user:\n\n1. MEV Exploitation: MEV bots can strategically delay user transactions in the mempool and execute them when prices are at their worst for the user. Searchers monitor pending transactions and can choose optimal timing for inclusion.\n\n2. Slippage Protection is Insufficient: While `calculatedAmountThreshold` bounds the immediate price impact relative to the pool state at execution time, it does NOT protect against absolute price level changes. A user expecting to swap at $2000/ETH may have their transaction delayed and executed at $1500/ETH - the slippage check passes (relative to the new price) but the user receives far less value than intended.\n\n3. Industry Standard Violation: All major DEX routers (Uniswap V2, Uniswap V3, Sushiswap, Curve, etc.) implement deadline protection for this exact reason. This is a well-established security pattern that Ekubo's Router omits.\n\n4. Universal Exposure: Every single Router swap user is exposed to this risk with no way to opt-out or protect themselves.\n\n5. Network Congestion Amplification: During periods of high network activity, transactions can sit in mempools for extended periods (hours or even days), dramatically increasing exposure to adverse price movements.\n\n\nScenario:\n1. Alice submits a swap transaction with 1% slippage protection when ETH = $2000\n2. Network congestion causes the transaction to sit in mempool for hours\n3. ETH price drops to $1500\n4. MEV bot sees Alice's stale transaction and strategically includes it\n5. Alice's swap executes at $1500 (within her 1% slippage of current price) but $500 worse than expected\n6. Alice receives significantly less value than intended when she submitted the transaction\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n\nAdd an optional `deadline` parameter to all swap functions and enforce it with a modifier:\n\n```solidity\nerror TransactionExpired();\n\nmodifier checkDeadline(uint256 deadline) {\n    if (deadline != 0 && block.timestamp > deadline) revert TransactionExpired();\n    _;\n}\n\nfunction swap(\n    PoolKey memory poolKey,\n    SwapParameters params,\n    int256 calculatedAmountThreshold,\n    uint256 deadline\n) public payable checkDeadline(deadline) returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate) {\n    // ... existing implementation\n}\n\nfunction multihopSwap(\n    Swap memory s,\n    int256 calculatedAmountThreshold,\n    uint256 deadline\n) public payable checkDeadline(deadline) returns (PoolBalanceUpdate[] memory balanceUpdates) {\n    // ... existing implementation\n}\n```\n\nThis follows the pattern established by other major DEX protocols like Uniswap V2/V3, which all include deadline parameters in their swap functions as a critical security measure.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n\nSave this POC in `test/poc/H01_MissingDeadlineProtection.t.sol`\n\nRun with:\n```bash\nforge test --match-contract H01_MissingDeadlineProtectionTest -v\n```\n\n### POC Code\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: ekubo-license-v1.eth\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {FullTest} from \"../FullTest.sol\";\nimport {Router, RouteNode, TokenAmount, Swap} from \"../../src/Router.sol\";\nimport {PoolKey} from \"../../src/types/poolKey.sol\";\nimport {SqrtRatio} from \"../../src/types/sqrtRatio.sol\";\nimport {PoolBalanceUpdate} from \"../../src/types/poolBalanceUpdate.sol\";\nimport {CoreLib} from \"../../src/libraries/CoreLib.sol\";\n\ncontract H01_MissingDeadlineProtectionTest is FullTest {\n    using CoreLib for *;\n\n    address alice;\n    address marketParticipant;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n        alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n        marketParticipant = makeAddr(\"marketParticipant\");\n\n        token0.transfer(alice, 100_000e18);\n        token1.transfer(alice, 100_000e18);\n        token0.transfer(marketParticipant, 1_000_000e18);\n        token1.transfer(marketParticipant, 1_000_000e18);\n    }\n\n    function test_H01_StaleTransactionExecutesAfterMarketMoves() public {\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createPool(0, 1 << 63, 100);\n        createPosition(poolKey, -10000, 10000, 10_000e18, 10_000e18);\n\n        uint256 aliceSwapAmount = 1000e18;\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        (PoolBalanceUpdate quoteAtSubmission,) = router.quote({\n            poolKey: poolKey,\n            isToken1: false,\n            amount: int128(uint128(aliceSwapAmount)),\n            sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0),\n            skipAhead: 0\n        });\n        uint256 expectedOutputAtSubmission = uint256(uint128(-quoteAtSubmission.delta1()));\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 hours);\n\n        vm.startPrank(marketParticipant);\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: int128(uint128(8_000e18))}),\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 aliceToken1Before = token1.balanceOf(alice);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: int128(uint128(aliceSwapAmount))}),\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n        uint256 actualOutput = token1.balanceOf(alice) - aliceToken1Before;\n\n        uint256 lossAmount = expectedOutputAtSubmission - actualOutput;\n        uint256 lossPercentageBps = (lossAmount * 10000) / expectedOutputAtSubmission;\n\n        assertLt(actualOutput, expectedOutputAtSubmission, \"Alice receives less than quoted\");\n        assertGt(lossAmount, 0, \"Alice suffered measurable loss\");\n        assertGt(lossPercentageBps, 0, \"Loss percentage is non-zero\");\n    }\n\n    function test_H01_TransactionExecutesAfterExtendedDelay() public {\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createPool(0, 1 << 63, 100);\n        createPosition(poolKey, -10000, 10000, 10_000e18, 10_000e18);\n\n        uint256 aliceSwapAmount = 500e18;\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        (PoolBalanceUpdate quoteAtSubmission,) = router.quote({\n            poolKey: poolKey,\n            isToken1: false,\n            amount: int128(uint128(aliceSwapAmount)),\n            sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0),\n            skipAhead: 0\n        });\n        uint256 expectedOutputAtSubmission = uint256(uint128(-quoteAtSubmission.delta1()));\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 7 days);\n\n        vm.startPrank(marketParticipant);\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: int128(uint128(8_000e18))}),\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 aliceToken1Before = token1.balanceOf(alice);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: int128(uint128(aliceSwapAmount))}),\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n        uint256 actualOutput = token1.balanceOf(alice) - aliceToken1Before;\n\n        uint256 lossAmount = expectedOutputAtSubmission - actualOutput;\n        uint256 lossPercentageBps = (lossAmount * 10000) / expectedOutputAtSubmission;\n\n        assertLt(actualOutput, expectedOutputAtSubmission, \"Stale transaction executes at degraded price\");\n        assertGt(lossAmount, 0, \"User suffered loss from delayed execution\");\n        assertGt(lossPercentageBps, 0, \"Loss is measurable\");\n    }\n\n    function test_H01_NoDeadlineParameterToPreventStaleExecution() public {\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createPool(0, 1 << 63, 100);\n        createPosition(poolKey, -1000, 1000, 10_000e18, 10_000e18);\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n\n        uint256 initialTimestamp = block.timestamp;\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 days);\n        router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: 100e18}),\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 30 days);\n        router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: 100e18}),\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 365 days);\n        router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: 100e18}),\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        assertGe(block.timestamp, initialTimestamp + 365 days, \"Swaps execute at any time - no deadline protection\");\n    }\n\n    function test_H01_MultihopSwapAlsoLacksDeadlineProtection() public {\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createPool(0, 1 << 63, 100);\n        createPosition(poolKey, -10000, 10000, 50_000e18, 50_000e18);\n\n        uint256 swapAmount = 2000e18;\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n\n        RouteNode[] memory route = new RouteNode[](1);\n        route[0] = RouteNode(poolKey, SqrtRatio.wrap(0), 0);\n\n        PoolBalanceUpdate[] memory resultsBefore = router.multihopSwap(\n            Swap(route, TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: int128(uint128(swapAmount))})),\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        uint256 outputBefore = uint256(uint128(-resultsBefore[0].delta1()));\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 days);\n\n        vm.startPrank(marketParticipant);\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        router.swap(\n            RouteNode({poolKey: poolKey, sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0), skipAhead: 0}),\n            TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: int128(uint128(40_000e18))}),\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        PoolBalanceUpdate[] memory resultsAfter = router.multihopSwap(\n            Swap(route, TokenAmount({token: address(token0), amount: int128(uint128(swapAmount))})),\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n        uint256 outputAfter = uint256(uint128(-resultsAfter[0].delta1()));\n\n        uint256 lossAmount = outputBefore - outputAfter;\n\n        assertLt(outputAfter, outputBefore, \"Multihop output degraded after delay\");\n        assertGt(lossAmount, 0, \"Multihop swap also lacks deadline protection\");\n    }\n}\n\n```",
